{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02400",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.55,
      "end_seconds": 6.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.57,
      "end_seconds": 13.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.45,
      "end_seconds": 18.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "It's electric shock pains in my cheek, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.98,
      "end_seconds": 30.16,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.75,
      "end_seconds": 51.52,
      "duration_seconds": 20.77,
      "text": "I'd say mild. It's on and off. I've also had being afraid to eat, for four weeks. Oh, and pain lasting seconds. Had that since yesterday. About pain lasting seconds, I'd say mild. It's a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 52.84,
      "end_seconds": 61.74,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. SpO2 97 percent on room air, pulse is 70 beats a minute, blood pressure 113 over 75."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.16,
      "end_seconds": 64.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.18,
      "end_seconds": 68.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.99,
      "end_seconds": 72.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.69,
      "end_seconds": 88.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "Touching the right cheek sets off the pain and the face muscles work normally."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.87,
      "end_seconds": 91.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.82,
      "end_seconds": 101.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Have you had any hearing loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.53,
      "end_seconds": 107.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "No, no hearing loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.71,
      "end_seconds": 110.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.16,
      "end_seconds": 113.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.14,
      "end_seconds": 135.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.88,
      "end_seconds": 141.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Okay, so no, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.61,
      "end_seconds": 149.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "So, have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.87,
      "end_seconds": 153.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.67,
      "end_seconds": 162.04,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "So, tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions. I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.7,
      "end_seconds": 168.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "I've had acid reflux for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.45,
      "end_seconds": 179.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Right, so acid reflux is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.27,
      "end_seconds": 199.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Right, now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.18,
      "end_seconds": 211.43,
      "duration_seconds": 11.25,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I swim twice a week. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.43,
      "end_seconds": 217.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Alright, do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.29,
      "end_seconds": 225.51,
      "duration_seconds": 7.22,
      "text": "It's something called lans... lansoprazole, 30 milligrams, maybe, before breakfast for my acidity."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.29,
      "end_seconds": 229.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.79,
      "end_seconds": 239.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Before this I was on omeprazole; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.87,
      "end_seconds": 256.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, I'd lean towards trigeminal neuralgia. Another possibility is a dental problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.75,
      "end_seconds": 259.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.79,
      "end_seconds": 291.0,
      "duration_seconds": 30.21,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like trigeminal neuralgia, but I'd like to confirm. We should do an MRI scan of the head for facial pain. You'll be taking carbamazepine, 100 milligrams, twice a day, titrate. That's for nerve pain. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Avoid known triggers and eat soft foods when it flares. I'll also refer you to the neurology clinic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.52,
      "end_seconds": 299.68,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.57,
      "end_seconds": 305.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Yeah, um, thank you, that's clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.51,
      "end_seconds": 314.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "I'll want another look in four weeks. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.07,
      "end_seconds": 319.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "I mean, good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}